Claude's last message: I built the `final` phone agent for the Turkish statement-debt case and saved it as version 10. In the last test it passed 2 of 2 cases, but that run only covered the latest fix. The full self-test sets were run on earlier versions and not repeated on version 10. **What it does:** the bank services (the card list and the e-mail lookup) are called by the workflow itself, not by the model. Code turns each card's balance into the finished Turkish reading the bank prescribes: - amounts in words, with full currency names, never TL, USD, EUR or GBP; - the last four digits read one by one, and no other digits of a card ever; - "another card?" before the offer; - the offer limited to what the caller can actually do; - the no-debt, new-card, cut-day and due-date wordings. The model only chooses which card, which week, and whether the caller said a clear yes. Every exit uses the bank's own closing sentences (main menu or customer representative), and all tool calls go to the mock. **Self-tests** (on the case's test customers, with Turkish callers): | Version | Cases | Result | |---|---|---| | 6 | smoke, then all 10 | 4/4, then 9/10 | | 7 | all 10 | 7/10 (one was a platform timeout, not the agent) | | 8 | 3 failed + 8 new paths | 9/11 | | 9 | 4 | 3/4 | | 10 | 2 (same name and same last four) | 2/2 | The failures were all fixed with small prompt changes: - the call looping when the caller kept talking after a closing sentence; - miscounting the three tries and the three calming replies by one; - digits said in two parts being counted as wrong answers; - reading a card when two cards share the same last four digits. Paths that passed include every service error, the joint statement, a supplementary card, a new card with no statement, the card name that contains an instruction, the first-digits request, an angry caller and the spouse's card. **Judgement calls you may want to review:** - **E-mail lookup failure:** that lookup must happen before the offer, an